    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.extra, mini.pick\n\n### Description\n\nHi @echasnovski, I've been using the LSP picker of **mini.extra** and are really happy about it. Since incoming and outgoing calls have Neovim API support, would it be possible to add support for these 2 features for the LSP picker?\r\n\r\nAfter browsing the code for this picker and the Neovim docs, it seems to me that the reason these are not implemented is due to `vim.lsp.buf.incoming_calls()` not allowing to pass an `opts` table like that of `vim.lsp.buf.references()`, and `opts.on_list` is used to start the picker. Similarly for `vim.lsp.buf.outgoing_calls()`. In this case, would it be possible to adopt some part of [Trouble](https://github.com/folke/trouble.nvim/blob/6efc446226679fda0547c0fd6a7892fd5f5b15d8/lua/trouble/sources/lsp.lua#L229)'s implementation?",
